    "slug": "manage-your-notion-links",
    "title": "Managing your Notion links",
    "html": "<p>The most important reason why we recommend that you sign-up for a free Notions11 account, is that you can manage all your Notion links after you have created them. In this tutorial we will show you how to do it, and what the benefits are.</p><p>First step is to <a href=\"https://www.notions11.com/signup\">sign-up for a free account</a>. In our blog \"<a href=\"https://www.notions11.com/blog/how-to-share-a-notion-link\">How to Share a Notion Link</a>\" we explained how you can share a Notion link without a registered Notions11 account, but once you have signed in you can see the Create New Link and the Manage Links button in the top menu. Let's start by creating a new link. Click on the Create New Link button, paste your Notion link and click on Next.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-image-card kg-card-hascaption\"><img src=\"https://jdtydxekoldfdysfyvyn.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog-images/ghost-images/2023/03/Screen1-4.jpg\" class=\"kg-image\" alt=\"Pasting a Notion link into the Notions11 Create New Link form\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1187\" height=\"498\" srcset=\"https://jdtydxekoldfdysfyvyn.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog-images/ghost-images/size/w600/2023/03/Screen1-4.jpg 600w, https://jdtydxekoldfdysfyvyn.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog-images/ghost-images/size/w1000/2023/03/Screen1-4.jpg 1000w, https://jdtydxekoldfdysfyvyn.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog-images/ghost-images/2023/03/Screen1-4.jpg 1187w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 720px) 720px\"><figcaption>Creating a new Notions11 link</figcaption></figure><p>As you can see, you can edit the Notions11 URL and the password, or simply use the automatically generated ones. After you have saved the link, you will be able to edit it by clicking on Manage Links. When you look at the action menu, you will see four options: Edit, Share, Preview and Delete.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-image-card\"><img src=\"https://jdtydxekoldfdysfyvyn.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog-images/ghost-images/2023/03/Screen2-7.jpg\" class=\"kg-image\" alt=\"Notions11 Manage Links action menu with Edit, Share, Preview and Delete options\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1243\" height=\"280\" srcset=\"https://jdtydxekoldfdysfyvyn.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog-images/ghost-images/size/w1000/2023/03/Screen2-7.jpg 1000w, https://jdtydxekoldfdysfyvyn.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/blog-images/ghost-images/2023/03/Screen2-7.jpg 1243w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 720px) 720px\"></figure><p>If you click on Edit, you can alter the URL of your link, and also change the password. The Share button lets you share the link by email. By clicking on Preview, you will see the screen that a recipient sees when your link is opened. You can also test your password before sharing it.</p><p>Setting an expiration date on a link is a Pro feature, so if you want to stop sharing the link, you can click on the Delete button.</p><p>If you want to test all the Pro features, such as expiring links, access notifications, branding and analytics, you can upgrade to Notions11 Pro and try the first 15 days for free.</p><div class=\"kg-card kg-button-card kg-align-center\"><a href=\"https://www.notions11.com/prosignup\">Upgrade to Notions11 Pro</a></div>",
